{"id":"G2017","lemma":"ἐπιφαύσκω","transliteration":"epiphauskō","sayIt":"epiphauskō","language":"Greek","partOfSpeech":"verb","gloss":"to shine on","meaning":"ἐπι-φαύσκω\n(variant form of ἐπιφώσκω, which see), [in LXX: Job.25:5 (אהל hi.) Job.31:26 41:18 (הָלַל hi.) * ;]\nto shine forth: figuratively, with dative, Eph.5:14 (on seel. -ψαύσει, see ICC, Westc., AR, in l).†\n(AS)","glosses":["will shine upon"],"count":1,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"eph-5","v":14,"renderings":{"kjv":"shall give"}}],"elsewhere":[{"ref":"Ephesians 5:14","note":"Therefore he says, “Awake, you who sleep, and arise from the dead, and Christ will shine on you.”","source":"web"}],"related":[{"id":"G20170","lemma":"ἀφόμοιος","transliteration":"aphomoios","gloss":"copy"},{"id":"G20171","lemma":"ἀφορολόγητος","transliteration":"aphorologētos","gloss":"untaxed"},{"id":"G20172","lemma":"ἀφρονεύομαι","transliteration":"aphroneuomai","gloss":"to act foolishly"},{"id":"G20173","lemma":"ἄφυκτος","transliteration":"aphuktos","gloss":"unable to escape"},{"id":"G20174","lemma":"ἀχανής","transliteration":"achanēs","gloss":"vast, immense"},{"id":"G20175","lemma":"ἀχρειότης","transliteration":"achreiotēs","gloss":"unprofitableness, worthlessness"},{"id":"G20176","lemma":"βαθύγλωσσος","transliteration":"bathuglōssos","gloss":"unintelligible"},{"id":"G20177","lemma":"βάϊς","transliteration":"bais","gloss":"bai"}],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}